}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105079 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105079 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bc8115e-85f8-522f-9b2b-266204228eb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105080 #edb/ref 1080 "55^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105080 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105080 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43f86416-172e-56a8-90f0-b9d9ddb827d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105081 #edb/ref 1080 "65^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105081 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105081 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c8ae4da-f6ca-5521-84b0-4b744cf4221a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105471 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12838" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105471 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the hexagon shown below. Draw an exterior angle of $\\angle B$.\n\n![](images/fc/fc1834e88b4d08a2705059d28d21105047898f251f0f2c29f8509be7b6321de0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0cd03b60-baf3-5689-9f84-5f8be9853a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105471 #edb/ref 1074 "To construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B$, we extend $\\overline{AB}$ past $B$. The angle between $\\overline{BC}$ and the extension of $\\overline{AB}$ is an exterior angle of $\\angle B$.\n\n![](images/d9/d91fc772042490e0785a4a617e4c3785c8616b7ed0ff05509ca8bc902eccc2a8.png)\n\nAnother way to construct an exterior angle of $\\angle B$ is to extend $\\overline{CB}$ past $B$. The angle between $\\overline{AB}$ and the extension of $\\overline{CB}$ is also an exterior angle of $\\angle B$.\n\n![](images/8d/8d031a6a6cc1513fc0a8031755b537d144279b88c964fc75728d3588ae1e4af9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105472 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105472 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/02/02ac83b8318d6067ba7959c390ccb8b011001ebcb289e4f31c27ba8e1ceb2913.png)\n\nIn the figure above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle{F}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105472 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbc903e6-45ee-53c5-9d31-0edf8140cacd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105472 #edb/ref 1074 "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $\\angle F$. Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n100^{∘} + 60^{∘} + 78^{∘} + 62^{∘} + x &= 360^{∘} \\\\\n300^{∘} + x &= 360^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 360^{∘} - 300^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 60^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105473 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12879" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105473 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0f/0f2d7f92335d965840f8714dc4ceeb43201ecee2ada9b7aeb7eb54437a0f7d0f.png)\n\nFind the value of $x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105473 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44ea9915-91ca-5abf-a1ac-bb801069ef24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105473 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $A$ is\n\n$$\n180^\\circ - 90^\\circ=90^\\circ\n$$\n\nand the measure of the exterior angle at $D$ is $180^\\circ - 2x$.\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n90^{∘} + (x + 10^{∘}) + (180^{∘} - 2x) + x + (x + 10^{∘}) &= 360^{∘} \\\\\nx + 290^{∘} &= 360^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 70^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105474 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105474 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/22/22130cbd3bb1f36d9ef8ce6290eead15354bbced7810e5fad5ac62972cd1d968.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle A$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e96a16e9-122f-582c-beb9-22ca0d4d7d68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105474 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^{\\circ}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(12x - 5^{∘}) + (6x + 5^{∘}) + (10x) + (9x - 10^{∘}) &= 360^{∘} \\\\\n37x - 10^{∘} &= 360^{∘} \\\\\n37x &= 360^{∘} + 10^{∘} \\\\\n37x &= 370^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 10^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $\\angle A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - 5^{∘} &= 12(10^{∘}) - 5^{∘} \\\\\n&= 120^{∘} - 5^{∘} \\\\\n&= 115^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Exterior Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105749 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9846ca00-8305-56a8-a14d-7aa2488c0016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating Exterior Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105750 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5de9bf2f-b11c-5af0-a569-5f25aebae227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105751 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105752 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1045 "Exterior Angles of Polygons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105975 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e068c66e-c6f9-5b98-88d1-321d4bd52ecb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106033 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106033 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106033 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/62/6252354d464db3c645186b9a8ef6001ee76408b04f7abf6a9046656270607085.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106033 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae89a7d0-62b6-55ff-a90b-0514ff252b15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106488 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186105076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106488 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106488 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ac/ac5d02edc0945574b5bf8f9a1112e9d7e9ca33ebc7714bfadcd14d02e46c43c7.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38b881c5-6a5a-5455-82f5-12615cde9f7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106643 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106643 #edb/ref 1061 187128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106643 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4bf926eb-9821-545f-b67e-d2d50c4f61f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106643 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106644 #edb/ref 1061 187129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106644 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d241585-6a66-55ed-8dd4-a690566db2a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106644 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106645 #edb/ref 1061 187132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80b138e7-13bc-505c-9c7b-e57531dd484d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106646 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106646 #edb/ref 1061 187135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106646 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c27f1faa-2fca-5dc4-8283-8cf462884593" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106646 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106647 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106647 #edb/ref 1061 187138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106647 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f65fca30-a9ac-5101-b87a-1c01743c0b0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106647 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106648 #edb/ref 1061 187141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ee786271-6101-5bf4-9d57-2fe763770d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107162 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the polygon $ABCD$, where the side $\\overline{AB}$ is extended beyond the vertex $B$.\n\n![](images/fa/fa23c036920e2c506c38f1e7be8a498c0a349ef145e8c444201665345bc648e4.png)\n\nWe call $\\color{blue}\\angle{CBE}$ the **exterior angle** of the vertex $B$.\n\nGiven a polygon's vertex, the interior and exterior angles are supplementary. So, for the vertex $B$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\color{YellowOrange}m\\angle{ABC}}_{\\large\\text{Interior}} \\:+\\: \\underbrace{\\color{blue}m\\angle{CBE}}_{\\large\\text{Exterior}} = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nWe have the following theorem:\n\n> The measures of the exterior angles of any simple polygon sum to $360^\\circ$.\n\nWe'll show why this theorem is true at the end of the lesson.\n\nLet's label the exterior angles of our polygon below:\n\n![](images/ac/acc0ac90f27a78e83b6b14651f61ddfe6a87afa56b6e51a1af57f5e74c31689f.png)\n\nAccording to our theorem, these four angles sum to $360^\\circ$.\n\n$$\na+b+c+d = 360^\\circ\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107162 #edb/ref 1065 8041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107162 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6cb4a5ba-6c28-59e2-ab72-89e4f5f69ae3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107162 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107163 #edb/ref 1064 "Why do the exterior angles of a polygon always sum to $360^\\circ$?\n\nSuppose we have an $n$-sided polygon. Then, we have the following:\n\n- There are $n$ pairs of interior-exterior angles, each pair being supplementary (i.e., their measures add to $180^\\circ)$.\n- Therefore, the sum of the measures of *all* interior-exterior pairs equals ${\\color{blue}n\\cdot 180^\\circ}$.\n- In a previous lesson, we saw that the sum of the *interior* angles equals ${\\color{red}{(n-2)\\cdot 180^\\circ}}$.\n\nTherefore, to get the sum of the *exterior* angles, we subtract ${\\color{red}{(n-2)\\cdot 180^\\circ}}$ from ${\\color{blue}n\\cdot 180^\\circ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nSum of Exterior Angles &= n \\cdot 180^{∘} - (n - 2) \\cdot 180^{∘} \\\\\n&= n \\cdot 180^{∘} - n \\cdot 180^{∘} + 2 \\cdot 180^{∘} \\\\\n&= n \\cdot 180^{∘} - n \\cdot 180^{∘} + 2 \\cdot 180^{∘} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 180^{∘} \\\\\n&= 360^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis proves that the sum of the exterior angles of a (simple) polygon equals $360^\\circ$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107163 #edb/ref 1065 8042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107163 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fb5a1532-47ec-5455-96c8-49187460e543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107163 #edb/ref 1067 "Proving the Theorem" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
